    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "The inequality $-4\\le x\\le -2$ can be expressed in interval notation as",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Every inequality can be expressed as an interval. We use the following notations:\n\n- Parentheses $()$ if the endpoints are *not* included.\n\n- Brackets $[]$ if the endpoints *are* included.\n\nOur inequality contains only \"or equal to\" symbols. So, the endpoints $-4$ and $-2$ *are* included. \n\n$$\n-4\\,\\,\\le \\,\\,x\\,\\,\\le \\,\\,-2\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express our inequality in interval notation as follows:\n\n$$\n[-4,-2]\n$$\n\nMore formally, we can also write\n\n$$\nx\\in [-4,-2].\n$$",
      ":question/id": "e71ef6b0-33d5-574b-a412-76bd2763d136",
